    "summary": "`sonar.sources` and `sonar.tests` both list `scripts`, but that directory does not exist in the repo, so the SonarCloud scanner stops with an error.",
    "failure_scenario": "CI with SONAR_TOKEN set → the scan step runs → the scanner reports \"The folder 'scripts' does not exist\" → the CI job turns red on every PR and every push to main."
  },
  {
    "file": "sonar-project.properties",
    "line": 5,
    "summary": "`sonar.sources=src` and `sonar.tests=src` overlap, and test files are never excluded from sources, so main and test files do not form separate sets.",
    "failure_scenario": "The first `src/**/*.spec.ts` is added → Sonar fails with \"File src/...spec.ts can't be indexed twice\". The fix is `sonar.exclusions` plus the test globs, or `sonar.test.inclusions` paired with a matching source exclusion."
  },
  {
    "file": "Dockerfile",
    "line": 17,
    "summary": "The adapter-node runtime sets no `ORIGIN` (or `PROTOCOL_HEADER`/`HOST_HEADER`), so behind Cloud Run's TLS proxy SvelteKit sees the app's origin as `http://...`.",
    "failure_scenario": "The MVP upload is a form action → the browser sends `Origin: https://gravespeaker-xxx.run.app` → SvelteKit compares it to the `http://` origin it inferred → 403 \"Cross-site POST form submissions are forbidden\"."
  },
  {
    "file": "Dockerfile",
    "line": 17,
    "summary": "`BODY_SIZE_LIMIT` is never set, so adapter-node keeps its 512K default request body limit, but the main PRD journey is uploading a phone photo of a headstone.",
    "failure_scenario": "A user uploads a typical 2–5 MB phone camera JPEG → adapter-node returns 413 Payload Too Large → the core 'Capture or upload' step fails for almost every real photo."
  },
  {
    "file": ".github/workflows/release-please.yml",
    "line": 10,
    "summary": "Release Please runs with `cancel-in-progress: true`, so a new push to main can kill a release run partway through.",
    "failure_scenario": "Two merges to main land in quick succession → the first run is cancelled after it creates the tag but before it creates the GitHub Release or updates the release PR labels → the state is inconsistent and the next run trips over it. Release workflows should use `cancel-in-progress: false`."
  },
  {
    "file": "deploy.sh",
    "line": 28,
    "summary": "The script deploys with `--service-account gravespeaker@...` and `--set-secrets` but never creates that service account, the secrets, or the `secretAccessor` binding.",
    "failure_scenario": "First run in a fresh project → `gcloud run deploy` fails because the service account does not exist, or because it lacks permission on secret `gemini-api-key`. The script enables Secret Manager and then assumes everything else is already there."
  },
  {
    "file": "Makefile",
    "line": 50,
    "summary": "The pre-commit `secret-scan` hook runs `gitleaks dir .`, which scans the whole working tree, not just staged or tracked files.",
    "failure_scenario": "Every commit scans node_modules, build, .svelte-kit, coverage and the untracked `.claude/` → commits are slow and secret-like strings in dependencies or Claude settings can block them. The `.gitleaks.toml` allowlist covers only `.env` and `.entire/metadata/`."
  },
  {
    "file": "Dockerfile",
    "line": 12,
    "summary": "The `prod-deps` stage is dead weight: package.json has no runtime `dependencies` because adapter-node bundles everything into `build/`, yet the image still installs and copies `node_modules`.",
    "failure_scenario": "Each build runs an extra pnpm install. With zero prod deps, `node_modules` may be empty or missing, which can make `COPY --from=prod-deps /app/node_modules` fail. Simpler form: drop the stage and copy only `build/` and `package.json`."
  },
  {
    "file": "lefthook.yml",
    "line": 1,
    "summary": "lefthook, actionlint and gitleaks are not declared anywhere (lefthook is not a devDependency and no `prepare` step installs hooks), so the hooks depend on tools already installed on the machine.",
    "failure_scenario": "On a fresh clone, `pnpm install` never installs git hooks, so no pre-commit, commit-msg or pre-push gate runs. This breaks the rule in ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md: \"No relying on 'already installed'.\""
  },
  {
    "file": ".github/dependabot.yml",
    "line": 11,
    "summary": "`open-pull-requests-limit: 1` breaks the user's rule in ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md: \"Prefer max open PR limit of 2 unless explicitly requested otherwise\" (the same value is on line 30).",
    "failure_scenario": "Any open Dependabot PR (for example, one stuck on a failing check) blocks every later update for that ecosystem, including security bumps."
  }
]
